/* Cyberpunk skin: neon lines on deep violet-black panels, cut corners, a
   magenta second accent and an acid third, after the reviewed skins mockup
   (stage 2; README.md next to this file). Every document links this sheet
   through nui/nui.rtpl, and every rule starts with .skin-cyberpunk, the
   body class of the cyberpunk theme (nui/theme/themes.json), so nothing
   here applies in a theme of another skin.

   Selector scheme (docs/ui/AUTHORING.md "Skins" and "Classic skin"): a rule
   takes the exact modern selector it overrides with .skin-cyberpunk in front,
   so it outweighs that rule by one class; components that can be the
   <body> itself list .skin-cyberpunk.x too. Layout stays the modern one to
   the pixel, but where the mockup's cyberpunk layout differs (the toggle's
   slanted track, the underlined tabs). Motion only on the chrome hooks the
   theme asks for (outline, corner-tl, corner-br, edge-top, scan, accent),
   transform and opacity only, values written out, every selector under
   600,000 (lint NUI011), and only on hooks that show: RmlUi advances an
   element's animation on every update even while it is hidden, so the
   motion rules name the window frame (or, in an overlay, the one board that
   shows the hook), not every hook. A board that is a document's <body>
   keeps the frame's hooks (the hide rules below name a board inside one).
   Filters, backdrop filters and masks only in .nui-fx rules (NUI010).
   Colors from the palette and the skin's tokens, lengths in dp.

   The only art is the white sprites of cyberpunk-sprites.rcss (the cut
   corner fills and outlines, the toggle's slanted track and knob, and the
   taskbar's HP ring; art.json), drawn as ninepatch decorators (the ring as
   a fill-image) and tinted by image-color from tokens, so they follow the
   player's colors. One element has one image-color, so a chip's fill and
   edge share their tint: the fill sprite's alpha is baked (chip 0.2, skew
   0.15), and a state changes the tint's alpha (the dim line at rest, the
   edge on hover, the solid accent pressed).
   No box-shadow: each one is a render target texture made the first time
   its element shows (a hitch on the device), and a device without effects
   would drop its element's background with it; glows are baked into the
   outline art or drawn as gradients. No text-transform: RmlUi 6.3 upper-cases
   ASCII letters only (ElementText.cpp), which would mix cases in most
   locales; the mockup's tracked capitals are tracked mixed case here. Item
   icons, skill icons and every other content image are never tinted. */

/* --- Window frame: the cut-corner panel ------------------------------------------
   The fill is the panel sprite (12dp cuts at the top right and bottom left)
   tinted with the panel color, so the player's panel color and opacity
   reach it. The frame keeps the modern 1dp border, transparent, so every
   window keeps its modern layout to the pixel; the fill covers the border
   box. A div frame is a stacking context (z-index 0), so the hooks drawn
   under the content (z-index -1) stay above the fill; a body frame is the
   document, which always is one. */
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-window, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window
{
	background-color: transparent;
	border-color: transparent;
	border-radius: 0;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-panel, cyberpunk-panel-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--surface);
}
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-window.nui-fx, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window.nui-fx
{
	box-shadow: none;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-window
{
	z-index: 0;
}
/* A band across the screen (the console): no cut corners, one neon line
   along its bottom. After the frame rule, which it ties. */
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-window--band, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window--band
{
	decorator: none;
	background-color: var(--surface-band);
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-dim);
}

/* --- Chrome hooks (docs/ui/AUTHORING.md "Chrome") -----------------------------------
   The runtime puts them as the first children of every frame and board
   (outline, corner-tl, corner-br, edge-top, scan) and title bar (accent)
   while this theme is in use; the component hides them, this sheet shows
   them. Their containing block is their frame's padding box, inside the
   frame's 1dp border. */

/* The neon outline: the panel's edge with a soft glow baked in, 6dp of glow
   outside the frame and 6dp inside, under the content. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-chrome--outline
{
	display: block;
	left: -7dp;
	top: -7dp;
	right: -7dp;
	bottom: -7dp;
	z-index: -1;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-panel-edge, cyberpunk-panel-edge-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge);
}

/* The two square corners: a 14dp bracket, magenta at the top left and in
   the accent at the bottom right, 3dp outside the frame, each pulsing from
   full to 0.55 opacity and back, the second half a cycle after the first,
   on window frames and on a document that is a board itself (the theme
   picker, the belt; other boards hide them, and the taskbar's overlay shows
   and moves its own). At rest (reduced motion) both show whole. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-chrome--corner-tl, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-chrome--corner-br
{
	display: block;
	box-sizing: border-box;
	width: 14dp;
	height: 14dp;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-chrome--corner-tl
{
	left: -4dp;
	top: -4dp;
	border-width: 2dp 0 0 2dp;
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-chrome--corner-br
{
	right: -4dp;
	bottom: -4dp;
	border-width: 0 2dp 2dp 0;
	border-color: var(--accent);
}
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-window > .nui-chrome--corner-tl.nui-anim, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window > .nui-chrome--corner-tl.nui-anim,
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-board > .nui-chrome--corner-tl.nui-anim
{
	animation: 2.4s sine-in-out infinite cyberpunk-pulse;
}
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-window > .nui-chrome--corner-br.nui-anim, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window > .nui-chrome--corner-br.nui-anim,
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-board > .nui-chrome--corner-br.nui-anim
{
	animation: 2.4s 1.2s sine-in-out infinite cyberpunk-pulse;
}
@keyframes cyberpunk-pulse
{
	0% { opacity: 1; }
	50% { opacity: 0.55; }
	100% { opacity: 1; }
}

/* The top edge's tab: a 44dp neon bar on the frame's top edge, 18dp from
   its left end, which every 6s runs along the edge toward the right end,
   shrinking to nothing as it goes, and grows back in place. The hook is as
   wide as the frame and draws the tab with a gradient, so a translate in
   percent moves it by the frame's width; it shrinks (scaleX about the
   tab's middle) instead of fading: an opacity change regenerates the
   gradient decorator, its shader and mesh, on every frame, a transform
   nothing. At rest (reduced motion) the tab stays in place, whole. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-chrome--edge-top
{
	display: block;
	left: -1dp;
	right: -1dp;
	top: -2dp;
	height: 3dp;
	decorator: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent 17dp, var(--accent) 18dp, var(--accent) 61dp, transparent 62dp);
	transform-origin: 40dp 50%;
	transform: translateX(0%) scaleX(1);
}
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-window > .nui-chrome--edge-top.nui-anim, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window > .nui-chrome--edge-top.nui-anim,
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-board > .nui-chrome--edge-top.nui-anim
{
	animation: 6s linear-in-out infinite cyberpunk-sweep;
}
@keyframes cyberpunk-sweep
{
	0% { transform: translateX(0%) scaleX(1); }
	55% { transform: translateX(0%) scaleX(1); }
	80% { transform: translateX(78%) scaleX(0); }
	81% { transform: translateX(0%) scaleX(0); }
	100% { transform: translateX(0%) scaleX(1); }
}

/* The holographic layer under the content: fine scan lines over a faint
   sheen, cyan in the top left corner and magenta in the bottom right one,
   clear between them, so the two cut corners stay clear. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-chrome--scan
{
	display: block;
	left: -1dp;
	top: -1dp;
	right: -1dp;
	bottom: -1dp;
	z-index: -1;
	decorator: repeating-linear-gradient(180deg, var(--cyberpunk-scan) 0dp, var(--cyberpunk-scan) 1dp, transparent 1dp, transparent 3dp),
		linear-gradient(135deg, var(--cyberpunk-holo-a) 0%, transparent 16%, transparent 84%, var(--cyberpunk-holo-b) 100%);
}

/* The title bar's accent: a short magenta bar on the bar's bottom line
   under the title's start, its glow a gradient across its 6dp. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-chrome--accent
{
	display: block;
	left: 12dp;
	bottom: -3dp;
	width: 28dp;
	height: 6dp;
	decorator: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent 0%, var(--cyberpunk-glow-alt) 30%, var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt) 42%, var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt) 58%, var(--cyberpunk-glow-alt) 70%, transparent 100%);
}

/* A band has no cut corners and no outline: its scan layer and its edge
   tab only. */
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-window--band > .nui-chrome--outline, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window--band > .nui-chrome--outline,
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-window--band > .nui-chrome--corner-tl, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window--band > .nui-chrome--corner-tl,
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-window--band > .nui-chrome--corner-br, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window--band > .nui-chrome--corner-br
{
	display: none;
}
/* Hidden there, so they do not pulse either (the frame rule's weight, later). */
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-window--band > .nui-chrome--corner-tl.nui-anim, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window--band > .nui-chrome--corner-tl.nui-anim,
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-window--band > .nui-chrome--corner-br.nui-anim, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window--band > .nui-chrome--corner-br.nui-anim
{
	animation: none;
}

/* --- Title bar, close button, footer ----------------------------------------------
   The modern bar (36dp) and body padding; the title a size smaller than
   modern's, tracked 0.5dp (so a long translated title takes the modern
   width) and lit, the bar's line the dim cyan line, no line above the
   footer. */

.skin-cyberpunk .nui-window__titlebar
{
	position: relative;
	border-bottom-color: var(--border);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-window__title
{
	color: var(--cyberpunk-title);
	font-size: 12dp;
	letter-spacing: 0.5dp;
	font-effect: glow(0dp 3dp 0dp 0dp var(--cyberpunk-glow));
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-window--compact .nui-window__title
{
	font-size: var(--font-sm);
	letter-spacing: 0.5dp;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-window__footer
{
	border-top-color: transparent;
}

/* --- Boards and tiles -------------------------------------------------------------
   A board is a small framed part of the HUD: the board fill (6dp cuts at
   the top left and bottom right), tinted with the panel color, and its
   outline hook as the board's 1dp neon edge. Boards are always loaded, so
   they show only the static outline by default; a window's overlay may
   show more on its boards. A board that is a document's <body> (the theme
   picker, the belt, the item tooltips) is drawn as a window frame. */
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-board, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-board
{
	background-color: transparent;
	border-color: transparent;
	border-radius: 0;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-board, cyberpunk-board-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--surface);
}
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-board
{
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-panel, cyberpunk-panel-inner) border-box;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-board
{
	z-index: 0;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-board > .nui-chrome--outline
{
	left: -1dp;
	top: -1dp;
	right: -1dp;
	bottom: -1dp;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-board-edge, cyberpunk-board-edge-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-dim);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-board > .nui-chrome--corner-tl, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-board > .nui-chrome--corner-br,
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-board > .nui-chrome--edge-top, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-board > .nui-chrome--scan
{
	display: none;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-board--notice, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-board--strip
{
	image-color: var(--notice-bar);
}
/* A tooltip board (the item, skill and link tooltips, and the refine and
   attach dialogs' item boards): the frame's cut shape on the shared overlay
   black (tip-bg, the player's overlay slot), the frame's neon outline, no
   shadow, and an acid bar down the top of its left edge. An inset board
   (inside a window) is opaque on the scene's color. */
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-board--tooltip, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-board--tooltip
{
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-panel, cyberpunk-panel-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--tip-bg);
}
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-board--tooltip.nui-fx, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-board--tooltip.nui-fx
{
	box-shadow: none;
}
/* An inset board sits in its window's flow, unpositioned; positioned, it
   holds its hooks (an unpositioned board's hooks would frame the window). */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-board--tooltip.nui-board--inset
{
	position: relative;
	image-color: var(--scene);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-board--tooltip > .nui-chrome--outline
{
	left: -7dp;
	top: -7dp;
	right: -7dp;
	bottom: -7dp;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-panel-edge, cyberpunk-panel-edge-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge);
}
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-board--tooltip > .nui-chrome--edge-top, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-board--tooltip > .nui-chrome--edge-top
{
	display: block;
	left: -1dp;
	top: -1dp;
	right: auto;
	width: 3dp;
	height: 36dp;
	decorator: none;
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-acid);
	transform: none;
}
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-board--tooltip > .nui-chrome--corner-tl, .skin-cyberpunk.nui-board--tooltip > .nui-chrome--corner-br,
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-board--tooltip > .nui-chrome--scan
{
	display: none;
}
/* A tooltip's hooks do not move (the frame rules' weight, later). */
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-board--tooltip > .nui-chrome--corner-tl.nui-anim, .skin-cyberpunk.nui-board--tooltip > .nui-chrome--corner-br.nui-anim,
.skin-cyberpunk.nui-board--tooltip > .nui-chrome--edge-top.nui-anim
{
	animation: none;
}
/* The ring and the disc are drawn by the minimap's overlay. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-board--ring
{
	decorator: none;
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-dim);
	border-radius: 9999dp;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-board--ring > .nui-chrome--outline
{
	display: none;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-tile
{
	background-color: var(--surface-raised);
	border-color: var(--border);
	border-radius: 0;
}

/* --- Panel, divider, badge -------------------------------------------------------
   Square panels: raised on the violet raised surface with the brighter cyan
   line, sunken in the well with the dim line, flat with a magenta line.
   Badges are acid tags. */

.skin-cyberpunk .nui-panel
{
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-dim);
	border-radius: 0;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-panel--sunken
{
	background-color: var(--surface-sunken);
	border-color: var(--border);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-panel--flat
{
	background-color: transparent;
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-glow-alt);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-panel__title
{
	color: var(--cyberpunk-title);
	letter-spacing: 1dp;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-divider
{
	border-top-color: var(--border);
}
/* The modern 18dp height, its edge inside it. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-badge
{
	height: 16dp;
	padding: 0 6dp;
	border-width: 1dp;
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-acid-line);
	border-radius: 0;
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-acid-soft);
	color: var(--cyberpunk-acid);
	font-weight: normal;
	line-height: 16dp;
	letter-spacing: 0.5dp;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-badge--accent
{
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-acid-soft);
	color: var(--cyberpunk-acid);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-badge--danger
{
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-acid-soft);
	color: var(--danger);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-badge--warning
{
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-acid-soft);
	color: var(--warning);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-badge--success
{
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-acid-soft);
	color: var(--success);
}

/* --- Buttons: chips cut at the bottom right ---------------------------------------
   The chip's fill (0.2) and its 1dp edge share one tint. Rest: the dim
   cyan line (the fill a faint 0.09). Hover: the brighter edge, white label.
   Press: the full accent. Keyboard focus: the acid edge alone. A selected
   choice: acid, fill, edge and label. Primary: the solid accent chip;
   danger: the magenta chip; ghost: no chip until hovered. The modern 1dp
   border stays, transparent, so sizes are the modern ones; labels are
   tracked 0.5dp (1dp ran long translations past the fixed-width choice
   rows of the system options). Rule order as classic's: the base and variants, then the
   states, each group after the one it must win against. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button
{
	background-color: transparent;
	border-color: transparent;
	border-radius: 0;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-chip, cyberpunk-chip-inner) border-box, ninepatch(cyberpunk-chip-edge, cyberpunk-chip-edge-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-dim);
	color: var(--text);
	letter-spacing: 0.5dp;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--primary
{
	background-color: transparent;
	border-color: transparent;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-chip-solid, cyberpunk-chip-solid-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--accent);
	color: var(--accent-text);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--danger
{
	background-color: transparent;
	border-color: transparent;
	image-color: var(--cyberpunk-glow-alt);
	color: var(--text);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--ghost
{
	background-color: transparent;
	border-color: transparent;
	decorator: none;
	color: var(--text-muted);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button[disabled], .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button:disabled
{
	opacity: 0.35;
}

.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button:hover, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button.is-hover
{
	background-color: transparent;
	image-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge);
	color: var(--cyberpunk-title);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button:active, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button.is-active
{
	background-color: transparent;
	image-color: var(--accent);
	color: var(--cyberpunk-title);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button:focus-visible, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button.is-focus
{
	border-color: transparent;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-chip-edge, cyberpunk-chip-edge-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--focus-ring);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button.is-selected
{
	background-color: transparent;
	border-color: transparent;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-chip, cyberpunk-chip-inner) border-box, ninepatch(cyberpunk-chip-edge, cyberpunk-chip-edge-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--cyberpunk-acid);
	color: var(--cyberpunk-acid);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--primary:hover, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--primary.is-hover
{
	border-color: transparent;
	image-color: var(--accent-hover);
	color: var(--accent-text);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--primary:active, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--primary.is-active
{
	border-color: transparent;
	image-color: var(--accent);
	color: var(--accent-text);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--danger:hover, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--danger.is-hover
{
	border-color: transparent;
	image-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt);
	color: var(--cyberpunk-title);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--danger:active, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--danger.is-active
{
	border-color: transparent;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-chip-solid, cyberpunk-chip-solid-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt);
	color: var(--accent-text);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--ghost:hover, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--ghost.is-hover
{
	border-color: transparent;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-chip, cyberpunk-chip-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge);
	color: var(--cyberpunk-title);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--ghost:active, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--ghost.is-active
{
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-chip, cyberpunk-chip-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--accent);
	color: var(--cyberpunk-title);
}
/* Focus over the variants (the modern rule of the same name): primary the
   solid chip with an acid notch in its cut (the background, which only the
   cut leaves uncovered; a dialog's default button has the focus when it
   opens), the others the acid edge. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--primary:focus-visible, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--primary.is-focus
{
	border-color: transparent;
	background-color: var(--focus-ring);
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-chip-solid, cyberpunk-chip-solid-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--accent);
	color: var(--accent-text);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--danger:focus-visible, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--ghost:focus-visible,
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--danger.is-focus, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--ghost.is-focus
{
	border-color: transparent;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-chip-edge, cyberpunk-chip-edge-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--focus-ring);
}
/* Icon buttons: square boxes with the glyph in the accent, untracked (the
   mockup's icon buttons are not cut). After the states, which they tie. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--icon
{
	decorator: none;
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-dim);
	color: var(--accent);
	font-size: var(--font-lg);
	letter-spacing: 0;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--small.nui-button--icon
{
	font-size: var(--font-md);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--icon:hover, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--icon.is-hover
{
	decorator: none;
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge);
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-holo-a);
	color: var(--accent-hover);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--icon:active, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--icon.is-active
{
	decorator: none;
	border-color: var(--accent);
	background-color: var(--selection);
	color: var(--accent-hover);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--icon:focus-visible, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--icon.is-focus
{
	decorator: none;
	border-color: var(--focus-ring);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--ghost.nui-button--icon
{
	border-color: transparent;
}
/* The compact title bar's close (the chat log): the glyph in the accent. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--icon-sm
{
	decorator: none;
	color: var(--accent);
	letter-spacing: 0;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--icon-sm:hover, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--icon-sm.is-hover,
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--icon-sm:focus-visible, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-button--icon-sm.is-focus
{
	background-color: transparent;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-chip, cyberpunk-chip-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--accent);
	color: var(--accent-hover);
}

/* A window's close: the modern 24dp ghost, its cross muted, magenta under
   the pointer, as the mockup's title bars show it. The title bar ancestor
   keeps each rule one class above the button rules of the same state. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-window__titlebar .nui-window__close
{
	border-color: transparent;
	decorator: none;
	color: var(--text-muted);
	font-weight: normal;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-window__titlebar .nui-window__close:hover, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window__titlebar .nui-window__close.is-hover
{
	border-color: transparent;
	background-color: transparent;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-chip, cyberpunk-chip-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt);
	color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-window__titlebar .nui-window__close:active, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window__titlebar .nui-window__close.is-active
{
	border-color: transparent;
	background-color: transparent;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-chip-solid, cyberpunk-chip-solid-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt);
	color: var(--accent-text);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-window__titlebar .nui-window__close:focus-visible, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window__titlebar .nui-window__close.is-focus
{
	border-color: var(--focus-ring);
	decorator: none;
}
/* A close drawn as the close glyph: the same inks. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-window__close .nui-glyph
{
	--glyph-ink: var(--text-muted);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-window__close:hover .nui-glyph, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window__close.is-hover .nui-glyph
{
	--glyph-ink: var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-window__close:active .nui-glyph, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window__close.is-active .nui-glyph
{
	--glyph-ink: var(--accent-text);
}

/* --- Text input: a dark well, a dim line and a brighter underline ----------- */

.skin-cyberpunk .nui-input
{
	background-color: var(--surface-sunken);
	border-color: var(--border);
	border-bottom-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-input:hover, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-input.is-hover
{
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-dim);
	border-bottom-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-input:focus, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-input.is-focus
{
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-dim);
	border-bottom-color: var(--accent);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-input--invalid, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-input--invalid:hover
{
	border-color: var(--danger);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-field__label, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-field__error
{
	letter-spacing: 1dp;
}

/* --- Toggle: a slanted track and knob --------------------------------------------
   The mockup's 32 x 14dp track and 10 x 8dp knob, both slanted (cut at the
   top left and bottom right). Off: the dim line and a muted knob; on: the
   accent's soft fill and line, the knob in the accent at the right end. The
   knob keeps the modern slide (its transition moves transform). */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-toggle__track
{
	width: 32dp;
	height: 14dp;
	border-color: transparent;
	border-radius: 0;
	background-color: transparent;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-skew-edge, cyberpunk-skew-edge-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-dim);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-toggle__knob
{
	left: 3dp;
	top: 2dp;
	width: 10dp;
	height: 8dp;
	border-radius: 0;
	background-color: transparent;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-knob, cyberpunk-knob-inner);
	image-color: var(--text-muted);
	transform: translateX(0dp);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-toggle:hover .nui-toggle__track, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-toggle.is-hover .nui-toggle__track
{
	border-color: transparent;
	image-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-toggle__input:checked + .nui-toggle__track
{
	border-color: transparent;
	background-color: transparent;
	decorator: ninepatch(cyberpunk-skew, cyberpunk-skew-inner) border-box, ninepatch(cyberpunk-skew-edge, cyberpunk-skew-edge-inner) border-box;
	image-color: var(--accent);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-toggle__input:checked + .nui-toggle__track .nui-toggle__knob
{
	background-color: transparent;
	image-color: var(--accent);
	transform: translateX(14dp);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-toggle__input:focus-visible + .nui-toggle__track, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-toggle.is-focus .nui-toggle__track
{
	border-color: transparent;
	image-color: var(--focus-ring);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-toggle__input:disabled + .nui-toggle__track, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-toggle__input:disabled + .nui-toggle__track + .nui-toggle__label
{
	opacity: 0.35;
}

/* --- Slider: a thin neon track, a magenta-to-cyan fill and a bar thumb ----------
   The fill is a vertex gradient (every device draws it); the thumb is the
   mockup's 6 x 16dp white bar inside a 2dp halo (a border, not a shadow). */

.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slider slidertrack
{
	margin-top: 8dp;
	height: 3dp;
	border-radius: 0;
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-holo-a);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slider sliderprogress
{
	border-radius: 0;
	background-color: var(--accent);
	decorator: horizontal-gradient(var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt) var(--accent));
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slider sliderbar
{
	margin-top: 0;
	width: 10dp;
	height: 20dp;
	border-width: 2dp;
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-glow);
	border-radius: 0;
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-title);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slider sliderbar:hover, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-slider.is-hover sliderbar
{
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-title);
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slider sliderbar:active, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-slider.is-active sliderbar
{
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-acid);
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-acid-line);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slider:focus-visible sliderbar, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-slider.is-focus sliderbar
{
	border-color: var(--focus-ring);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slider:disabled
{
	opacity: 0.35;
}

/* --- Tabs: tracked labels over one line, the selected one underlined -------------
   The mockup's underlined tabs on the modern 32dp: a 5dp gap above 26dp
   tabs and the row's dim line. The selected tab lights its label, lifts a
   soft cyan from the line (a vertex gradient) and takes a magenta
   underline; the indicator, hidden in modern, is that 2dp underline and
   slides with the modern motion where the tabset has one. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-tabs tabs
{
	gap: 0;
	padding: 5dp 0 0 0;
	border-width: 0 0 1dp 0;
	border-color: var(--border);
	border-radius: 0;
	background-color: transparent;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-tabs tab
{
	height: 26dp;
	border-radius: 0;
	color: var(--text-muted);
	line-height: 24dp;
	letter-spacing: 1dp;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-tabs tab:hover, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-tabs tab.is-hover
{
	color: var(--text);
	background-color: transparent;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-tabs tab:selected
{
	color: var(--cyberpunk-title);
	background-color: transparent;
	border-color: transparent;
	border-bottom-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt);
	decorator: vertical-gradient(transparent var(--cyberpunk-holo-a));
	font-effect: glow(0dp 3dp 0dp 0dp var(--cyberpunk-glow));
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-tabs tab:focus-visible, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-tabs tab.is-focus
{
	border-color: var(--focus-ring);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-tabs tab.nui-tabs__indicator
{
	display: block;
	bottom: -1dp;
	height: 2dp;
	padding: 0;
	border-width: 0;
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt);
	decorator: none;
	font-effect: none;
	line-height: 0;
}

/* --- List: square rows, the selected one marked in magenta ------------------------ */

.skin-cyberpunk .nui-list__item
{
	border-radius: 0;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-list__item.is-selected
{
	border-color: transparent;
	border-left-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt);
	color: var(--cyberpunk-title);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-list__item:focus-visible, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-list__item.is-focus
{
	border-color: var(--focus-ring);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-list__item.is-selected:focus-visible, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-list__item.is-selected.is-focus
{
	border-left-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-list__meta
{
	letter-spacing: 1dp;
}

/* --- Slot grid: square cells with a faint cyan fill and line ----------------------
   Hover the accent's soft fill and line, selected magenta, an active item
   acid; counts in acid. The icons themselves are never tinted. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot
{
	border-radius: 0;
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-cell);
	border-color: var(--border);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot:hover, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot.is-hover
{
	background-color: var(--selection);
	border-color: var(--accent);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot.is-selected
{
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-holo-b);
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot__cover, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot__ring
{
	border-radius: 0;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot__count, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot__number .nui-number__text
{
	border-radius: 0;
	color: var(--cyberpunk-acid);
}
/* The lean grid (P14 spec 4.2): its bases square with the faint fill and
   line, in one draw; a lean cell draws nothing at rest, and the states
   below light it. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot-grid--lean
{
	decorator: nui-cells(40dp 4dp 0dp var(--cyberpunk-cell) var(--border) 1dp);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot
{
	background-color: transparent;
	border-color: transparent;
}
/* After the rule above, which they outweigh: each state's fill and edge. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot:hover, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-hover
{
	background-color: var(--selection);
	border-color: var(--accent);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-picked
{
	background-color: var(--slot-picked);
	border-color: var(--accent);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-target
{
	background-color: var(--slot-target);
	border-color: var(--accent);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-active
{
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-acid);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot.is-unavailable, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot.is-unavailable:hover,
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-unavailable, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-unavailable:hover
{
	background-color: var(--slot-unavailable);
	border-color: var(--border);
}

/* --- Gauges: square, segmented, lit from the top ----------------------------------
   The fill's color with a white sheen fading down (a vertex gradient, which
   every device draws) under dark segment gaps every 8dp (a repeating
   gradient whose first and last stops are clear, so a device without
   effects draws none; RmlUi does not keep the order of two stops at one
   position, so no two stops share one). The first decorator draws on top. */
.skin-cyberpunk progress.nui-gauge
{
	border-radius: 0;
	background-color: var(--gauge-track);
}
.skin-cyberpunk progress.nui-gauge fill
{
	border-radius: 0;
	decorator: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, transparent 0dp, transparent 6.9dp, var(--surface-sunken) 7dp, var(--surface-sunken) 7.9dp, transparent 8dp),
		vertical-gradient(var(--sheen) var(--sheen-clear));
}

/* --- Tooltip: the shared overlay black with a neon line ---------------------------- */

.skin-cyberpunk .nui-tooltip
{
	border-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge);
	border-radius: 0;
	background-color: var(--tooltip-bg);
	color: var(--text-inverse);
	font-effect: shadow(0dp 1dp var(--text-outline));
}

/* --- Scrollbars: a thin neon thumb --------------------------------------------------- */

.skin-cyberpunk scrollbarvertical sliderbar
{
	border-radius: 0;
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-dim);
}
.skin-cyberpunk scrollbarhorizontal sliderbar
{
	border-radius: 0;
	background-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-dim);
}
.skin-cyberpunk scrollbarvertical sliderbar:hover, .skin-cyberpunk scrollbarvertical sliderbar:active,
.skin-cyberpunk scrollbarhorizontal sliderbar:hover, .skin-cyberpunk scrollbarhorizontal sliderbar:active
{
	background-color: var(--accent);
}

/* --- Modal backdrop: the world blurred behind a dialog ----------------------------
   A layer on every frame while a modal shows; reduced effects takes the blur
   off (base.rcss) and leaves the scrim's tint. */
body.skin-cyberpunk.nui-scrim.nui-fx
{
	backdrop-filter: blur(4dp);
}

/* --- Glyphs and links ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

.skin-cyberpunk .nui-glyph
{
	--glyph-ink: var(--accent);
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-link:hover
{
	text-decoration: underline;
}

/* --- Reduced effects ----------------------------------------------------------------
   The look a device without effects also shows: no scan layer (gradients
   would draw one flat color there), the edge tab and the title accent as
   plain bars, the tab resting. */
@media (theme: reduced-effects)
{
	.skin-cyberpunk .nui-chrome--scan
	{
		display: none;
	}
	.skin-cyberpunk .nui-chrome--edge-top
	{
		left: 17dp;
		right: auto;
		width: 44dp;
		decorator: none;
		background-color: var(--accent);
		transform: none;
	}
	/* Plain, so it rests (the frame rule's weight, later). */
	.skin-cyberpunk.nui-window > .nui-chrome--edge-top.nui-anim, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-window > .nui-chrome--edge-top.nui-anim,
	.skin-cyberpunk.nui-board > .nui-chrome--edge-top.nui-anim
	{
		animation: none;
	}
	.skin-cyberpunk .nui-chrome--accent
	{
		bottom: -1dp;
		height: 2dp;
		decorator: none;
		background-color: var(--cyberpunk-edge-alt);
	}
}

/* --- Wave 3c (P15) ------------------------------------------------------------------- */

/* A skill cell's plus button: square; its glyph in the accent's text color
   (the skin inks every other glyph in the accent). */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot-button
{
	border-radius: 0;
}
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot-button .nui-glyph
{
	--glyph-ink: var(--accent-text);
}
/* The refine's closed cell: no hover light. */
.skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot.is-closed:hover, .skin-cyberpunk .nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-closed:hover
{
	background-color: var(--slot-unavailable);
	border-color: var(--border);
	decorator: none;
}
